{
  "slug": "artist:vybz-kartel",
  "name": "Vybz Kartel",
  "editorial_article": "Born Adidja Azim Palmer in Kingston, Jamaica, Vybz Kartel launched his professional music career in 1993 with the debut single 'Love Fat Woman' released on the One Heart label. A central figure in the Jamaican dancehall scene, Kartel became a protege of Bounty Killer before forming his own collective, the Portmore Empire. Throughout his career, he has collaborated with artists including Major Lazer, Rihanna, Missy Elliott, and Travis Scott. His 2016 album 'King of the Dancehall' peaked at number two on the Billboard Reggae Chart and featured the hit single 'Fever', which was certified Gold in the United Kingdom in 2026. Kartel is known for his business ventures, including the launch of Street Vybz Rum and his own footwear line, Addi's.",
